board:0026 emulated-time stamps -- every FIST_WATCHPHYS/FIST_WATCHFLAT line ends in " t=<ms>" (PIC_FullIndex)
and every 9200 pass capture line is preceded by "[r92cam-now t=<ms>] ", so writes and windshield frames
can be related to time: the oracle's in-mission frame rate (scratch/oracle/fps: 25.7 fps on this host,
0 or 1 frames per [0x452] tick) came from a FIST_WATCHPHYS on [0x452] (phys 0x2d5e2) plus
FIST_R9200CAP=1 FIST_R92_NOMEMARM=1 FIST_R9200MAX=100000 in one run.  Also arms FIST_R9200CAP from the
FIST_MEMARM_BOOT constructor (the lazy init that used to read it never ran once the boot arm had set
fist_inited).  Apply to third_party/dosbox-build/dosbox-0.74-3/src/hardware/vga_memory.cpp, then `make`.
--- a/src/hardware/vga_memory.cpp
+++ b/src/hardware/vga_memory.cpp
@@ -227,6 +227,7 @@
